        "title": "Display multiple graphs as distinct, usable documents in one workspace",
        "body": "Goal: Display multiple graphs as distinct, usable documents in one workspace\nStatus: todo\n\nTasks in scope:\n1. Create the multi-document workspace state model\n2. Render visible graph regions and headers\n3. Define graph activation and focus behavior\n4. Map graph-local coordinates into the workspace\n\nOpen questions:\n1. When should workspace state become a graph artifact?\n2. What is the supported open-graph budget?\n3. How much automatic graph placement is useful?",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "startedAt": "",
        "completedAt": "",
        "externalRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/tasks/multi-graph-workspace/root.node",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "Two or more graph documents can be visible at the same time with unmistakable borders and headers.",
          "Exactly one graph is active, and all edit, save, undo, and keyboard commands resolve to it.",
          "Cross-graph edges remain visually continuous while persistence lands in the correct declaration-owned files.",
          "Opening one graph still works as a one-region workspace with no regression in the existing flow."
        ]
      }
