    {
      "id": "multi-graph-workspace-landing-surface",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "Multi-Graph Workspace Specification",
      "position": {
        "x": 80,
        "y": -1320
      },
      "width": 760,
      "height": 560,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Multi-Graph Workspace\n\nOpen, compare, connect, and edit several graph documents without losing the boundary of any one graph.\n\n## The visual rule\n\nEvery graph is rendered inside a persistent, labeled frame. The active graph gets a strong accent border and focus mark. Inactive graphs retain a visible neutral border. Dirty, loading, failed, and read-only states live in the frame header. Cross-graph edges draw above the frames and show small transition markers where they cross a graph boundary.\n\n## The interaction rule\n\nOne graph is active at a time. Clicking anywhere inside a graph activates it; clicking its empty surface clears node focus and ends handle editing. Clicking outside all graphs also clears node focus while retaining the last active graph so Save, Undo, and Add remain deterministic.\n\n## The document rule\n\nEach region remains a separately authoritative graph. Node coordinates remain graph-local. Save targets the active graph; Save All visits dirty graphs independently. Cross-graph edge references remain in their owning files. Workspace arrangement is stored separately from graph content.\n\n## Delivery slices\n\n1. Workspace state, two graph regions, visible borders, activation, and Fit Active / Fit Workspace.\n2. Editing, dirty state, per-graph undo/redo, active Save, and Save All.\n3. Cross-graph edge overlay, boundary markers, selection, and persistence.\n4. Restore workspace layout, virtualization, accessibility, and capacity limits."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "multi-graph-workspace-declaration"
        }
      }
    },
