        "title": "Add open-alongside, close, and load lifecycle",
        "body": "Make Open Alongside a distinct navigation action from replace-current and same-node expansion. New regions begin with a visible loading shell; failures stay contained in that region; closing a dirty graph uses the existing save/discard flow.",
        "priority": "high",
        "status": "todo",
        "owner": "",
        "estimateHours": "12",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "A portal or browser action can open a graph beside the current graph.",
          "Loading and failure states keep the region border and graph identity visible.",
          "Closing one region does not navigate or reload the remaining graphs.",
          "Duplicate graph opens receive separate workspace instance IDs."
        ],
