          "angle": 270
        }
      ],
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "input",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 270,
          "portId": "root"
        }
      ],
      "inputs": [
        {
          "key": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "type": "any"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Acceptance contract\n\n## Always visible\n\n- Every open graph has a border and header, including loading and error states.\n- Active state is signaled by border weight, accent, and an ACTIVE badge.\n- Dirty and read-only states are attached to the owning graph header.\n\n## Always scoped\n\n- One graph owns each local node coordinate and mutation.\n- One active graph receives commands.\n- Node focus may be empty while active graph scope remains set.\n- Workspace arrangement never dirties a graph document.\n\n## Cross-graph\n\n- Cross-graph edges render in a workspace overlay and remain selectable.\n- Boundary markers explain the transition without impersonating semantic ports.\n- Each graph persists only the references and segments it owns.\n\n## Backward compatibility\n\n- Existing single-graph navigation opens one full workspace region.\n- Same-node expansion remains distinct from Open Alongside.\n- Save keeps its focused-graph ownership contract; Save All remains explicit."
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "receivesViewContent": true
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "multi-graph-workspace-declaration"
        }
      }
    }
  ],
